{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-22T02:37:53.759Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"Here’s what each step does and why it’s useful.\n\n```r\ncolnames(annot)[1] <- \"probe\"\n```\n\nRenames the first column of `annot` from `probe_id` to `probe`. The two tables need a column with the same name so `merge()` can use it as their shared key. This changes `annot` in place.\n\n```r\nmerged <- merge(results, annot, by = \"probe\", all.x = TRUE)\n```\n\nJoins the annotation onto each row of `results`, matching rows by probe ID. `all.x = TRUE` means “keep every row from `results`,” even when there is no annotation match. Those unmatched probes get `NA` for `symbol`.\n\nThat matters because `results` is your set of tested probes; dropping a probe just because its annotation is missing would discard its result. Also, multiple probes can map to the same symbol, so a join can legitimately produce multiple rows with that symbol. By default, `merge()` sorts the output by the key.\n\n```r\nannotated <- merged[!is.na(merged$symbol) & merged$symbol != \"\", ]\n```\n\nKeeps rows whose symbol is neither `NA` nor an empty string. These are two different ways missing annotations appear in your data, so both checks are needed. This leaves probes with usable gene symbols.\n\n```r\nsig <- annotated[annotated$adj.P.Val < 0.05, ]\n```\n\nKeeps rows with adjusted p-value below 0.05. The adjusted values account for testing many probes, making them more appropriate for deciding significance across the whole analysis than raw `P.Value`.\n\n```r\nsig$direction <- ifelse(sig$logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")\n```\n\nAdds a `direction` column based on the sign of `logFC`: positive means higher expression in the numerator or comparison group, and negative means lower. The labels “up” and “down” depend on how the original comparison was set up.\n\n```r\nsig <- sig[order(sig$adj.P.Val), ]\n```\n\nSorts the significant rows from smallest to largest adjusted p-value. This puts the strongest statistical evidence first.\n\n```r\nbest <- sig[!duplicated(sig$symbol), ]\n```\n\nKeeps only the first row for each symbol, so a gene represented by multiple significant probes appears once. Because `sig` was just sorted by adjusted p-value, this keeps the probe with the smallest adjusted p-value for each symbol. For example, both `1001_at` and `1002_s_at` map to `NPPA`; this keeps `1001_at`.\n\n```r\nrownames(best) <- NULL\n```\n\nResets the row names after filtering. Otherwise, `best` may retain row numbers from earlier tables, which can look irregular. This affects display only, not the data.\n\n```r\nnrow(merged); nrow(annotated); nrow(sig); nrow(best)\n```\n\nPrints the row count after each filtering stage, helping you see how many rows were retained or removed at each point. In this example, the counts should be `10`, `8`, `6`, and `5`, respectively: 10 result probes, 8 with symbols, 6 significant annotated probes, and 5 unique significant symbols.\n\n```r\nbest\ntable(best$direction)\n```\n\nDisplays the final one-row-per-symbol table, then counts how many of those genes are classified as up or down. For the values shown, `NPPA` and `FRZB` are up, while `MYH6`, `SERPINA3`, and `CORIN` are down.","date":"2026-11-22T02:38:19.981Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1.chat","acp_log_key":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578:76846e83-1c41-44fe-b2d7-81524e73c0a5","acp_log_subject":"project.b340ce06-0bbf-48c4-b6f7-44b8df7532cf.acp-log.1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578.76846e83-1c41-44fe-b2d7-81524e73c0a5","acp_started_at_ms":1795315074905,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/10_GeneEnrichment","acp_account_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"76846e83-1c41-44fe-b2d7-81524e73c0a5","thread_id":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578","parent_message_id":"5b91764e-f3f6-467f-bcbb-327f070348da","acp_thread_id":"01a09ce8-cd32-7560-baed-cc49038ff81b","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":28314,"cached_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1282,"reasoning_output_tokens":516,"total_tokens":29596,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-22T02:49:27.734Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"```r\n# Rename annot's first column so it matches the probe key in results.\n# merge() uses this shared column to match each result to its annotation.\ncolnames(annot)[1] <- \"probe\"\n\n# Add annotations to results, keeping every probe from results.\n# Probes without a matching annotation are retained with NA for symbol.\nmerged <- merge(results, annot, by = \"probe\", all.x = TRUE)\n\n# Keep rows with a usable symbol: exclude both NA and empty-string symbols.\nannotated <- merged[!is.na(merged$symbol) & merged$symbol != \"\", ]\n\n# Keep genes whose multiple-testing-adjusted p-value is below 0.05.\nsig <- annotated[annotated$adj.P.Val < 0.05, ]\n\n# Label the direction of change from the sign of the log fold change.\nsig$direction <- ifelse(sig$logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")\n\n# Sort by adjusted p-value so the strongest statistical evidence comes first.\nsig <- sig[order(sig$adj.P.Val), ]\n\n# Keep one probe per symbol. Since sig is sorted, this keeps the probe\n# with the smallest adjusted p-value when several probes share a symbol.\nbest <- sig[!duplicated(sig$symbol), ]\n\n# Reset row names after filtering so they run consecutively from 1.\nrownames(best) <- NULL\n\n# Show the number of rows at each stage to track how filtering changes the data.\nnrow(merged); nrow(annotated); nrow(sig); nrow(best)\n\n# Display the final table and count its genes by direction of change.\nbest\ntable(best$direction)\n```","date":"2026-11-22T02:49:41.140Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1.chat","acp_log_key":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578:9bd1f3c3-425b-44c7-a0eb-6d1b53768308","acp_log_subject":"project.b340ce06-0bbf-48c4-b6f7-44b8df7532cf.acp-log.1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578.9bd1f3c3-425b-44c7-a0eb-6d1b53768308","acp_started_at_ms":1795315769663,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/10_GeneEnrichment","acp_account_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"9bd1f3c3-425b-44c7-a0eb-6d1b53768308","thread_id":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578","parent_message_id":"150310b7-6fc4-4463-a79f-baaf4b488634","acp_thread_id":"01a09ce8-cd32-7560-baed-cc49038ff81b","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":32401,"cached_input_tokens":28311,"output_tokens":716,"reasoning_output_tokens":369,"total_tokens":33117,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-22T02:50:52.365Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"This version starts from the existing `results` and `annot` objects. It renames a copy of `annot` for the join, so neither input is changed, and it does not modify `best`.\n\n```r\n# Rename the annotation key for the join; this creates annot_tidy\n# and leaves the original annot unchanged.\nannot_tidy <- annot %>%\n  rename(probe = probe_id)\n\n# Add annotations while retaining every probe from results.\nmerged_tidy <- results %>%\n  left_join(annot_tidy, by = \"probe\")\n\n# Keep rows with a non-missing, non-empty gene symbol.\nannotated_tidy <- merged_tidy %>%\n  filter(!is.na(symbol), symbol != \"\")\n\n# Keep statistically significant rows, label change direction,\n# and sort so the smallest adjusted p-values come first.\nsig_tidy <- annotated_tidy %>%\n  filter(adj.P.Val < 0.05) %>%\n  mutate(direction = if_else(logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")) %>%\n  arrange(adj.P.Val)\n\n# Keep one probe per symbol. Because the rows are sorted by adjusted\n# p-value, this retains the most significant probe for each symbol.\nbest_tidy <- sig_tidy %>%\n  distinct(symbol, .keep_all = TRUE)\n\n# Show how many rows remain after each stage.\ntibble(\n  stage = c(\"merged\", \"annotated\", \"significant\", \"unique symbols\"),\n  n = c(\n    nrow(merged_tidy),\n    nrow(annotated_tidy),\n    nrow(sig_tidy),\n    nrow(best_tidy)\n  )\n)\n\n# Display the final table and count genes by direction.\nbest_tidy\nbest_tidy %>%\n  count(direction)\n```\n\nTibbles don’t need row names reset: they display row numbers automatically. With the example data, the stage counts should be 10, 8, 6, and 5.","date":"2026-11-22T02:51:08.006Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1.chat","acp_log_key":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578:591f2683-3120-4c21-b11b-4e2f81718c42","acp_log_subject":"project.b340ce06-0bbf-48c4-b6f7-44b8df7532cf.acp-log.1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578.591f2683-3120-4c21-b11b-4e2f81718c42","acp_started_at_ms":1795315853693,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/10_GeneEnrichment","acp_account_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"591f2683-3120-4c21-b11b-4e2f81718c42","thread_id":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578","parent_message_id":"19d1ad0a-d834-4358-9deb-fb170c50f82f","acp_thread_id":"01a09ce8-cd32-7560-baed-cc49038ff81b","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":35957,"cached_input_tokens":32398,"output_tokens":1437,"reasoning_output_tokens":1021,"total_tokens":37394,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-22T02:55:41.516Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"Two common alternatives are:\n\n1. **Aggregate the probe sets:** For each gene, average or take the median of its probe-set expression values across samples, then perform the differential-expression analysis on that gene-level value. This combines the probes instead of choosing one.\n\n2. **Choose the most variable probe set:** Keep the probe set with the largest variance across samples, on the idea that it may best capture meaningful differences. This rule is sensitive to outliers and can select noise, so it’s usually worth checking the probe’s quality and annotation too.","date":"2026-11-22T02:55:48.884Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/.local/share/cocalc/navigator-135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1.chat","acp_log_key":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578:061f7df9-f103-45fd-99f0-816329536ca7","acp_log_subject":"project.b340ce06-0bbf-48c4-b6f7-44b8df7532cf.acp-log.1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578.061f7df9-f103-45fd-99f0-816329536ca7","acp_started_at_ms":1795316143045,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/10_GeneEnrichment","acp_account_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"061f7df9-f103-45fd-99f0-816329536ca7","thread_id":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578","parent_message_id":"97c5a84b-a1ae-4815-b6f7-42b300dd9fa2","acp_thread_id":"01a09ce8-cd32-7560-baed-cc49038ff81b","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":40225,"cached_input_tokens":35954,"output_tokens":395,"reasoning_output_tokens":279,"total_tokens":40620,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
