{"sender_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","content":"Here is results output: A data.frame: 10 × 4\nprobe\tlogFC\tP.Value\tadj.P.Val\n<chr>\t<dbl>\t<dbl>\t<dbl>\n1001_at\t2.10\t2e-09\t1.0e-06\n1002_s_at\t1.40\t4e-06\t3.0e-04\n1003_at\t-1.35\t6e-06\t4.0e-04\n1004_at\t-1.39\t1e-12\t2.0e-09\n1005_at\t1.01\t9e-10\t8.0e-07\n1006_x_at\t0.30\t8e-02\t2.1e-01\n1007_at\t0.90\t2e-05\t1.0e-03\n1008_at\t-0.80\t4e-05\t2.0e-03\n1009_at\t0.02\t9e-01\t9.5e-01\n1010_at\t-0.70\t5e-04\t1.2e-02\n  \n  Here is annot output: A data.frame: 9 × 2\nprobe_id\tsymbol\n<chr>\t<chr>\n1001_at\tNPPA\n1002_s_at\tNPPA\n1003_at\tMYH6\n1004_at\tSERPINA3\n1005_at\tFRZB\n1006_x_at\tFRZB\n1007_at\t\n1009_at\tGAPDH\n1010_at\tCORIN\n  \n  Here is the code: colnames(annot)[1] <- \"probe\"\nmerged <- merge(results, annot, by = \"probe\", all.x = TRUE)\nannotated <- merged[!is.na(merged$symbol) & merged$symbol != \"\", ]\nsig <- annotated[annotated$adj.P.Val < 0.05, ]\nsig$direction <- ifelse(sig$logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")\nsig <- sig[order(sig$adj.P.Val), ]\nbest <- sig[!duplicated(sig$symbol), ]\nrownames(best) <- NULL\n\nnrow(merged); nrow(annotated); nrow(sig); nrow(best)\nbest\ntable(best$direction)\n                  \n    Please explain why each step in the code is there, in addition to its function. I already have a basic understanding of R.","date":"2026-11-22T02:37:53.551Z"}],"date":"2026-11-22T02:37:53.551Z","message_id":"5b91764e-f3f6-467f-bcbb-327f070348da","thread_id":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","content":"he code keeps, for each gene, the probe set with the smallest adjusted p-value.. What are two other rules people use when several probe sets map to one gene","date":"2026-11-22T02:55:41.413Z"}],"date":"2026-11-22T02:55:41.413Z","message_id":"97c5a84b-a1ae-4815-b6f7-42b300dd9fa2","thread_id":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578","parent_message_id":"591f2683-3120-4c21-b11b-4e2f81718c42","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"135c8a4a-2bce-4f8a-94cc-4578a1eeb4f1","content":"rewrite the same steps using tidyverse functions and the pipe, with comments. the final table must be called best_tidy. it must start from results and annot as they are now, and must not change best","date":"2026-11-22T02:50:52.345Z"}],"date":"2026-11-22T02:50:52.345Z","message_id":"19d1ad0a-d834-4358-9deb-fb170c50f82f","thread_id":"1c1b9e64-0844-4bd2-aa41-d1543491d578","parent_message_id":"9bd1f3c3-425b-44c7-a0eb-6d1b53768308","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}